  "idea": "How to split your computer screen into two clean windows for multitasking",
  "text": "This essential desktop organization trick is something every beginner needs on day one. Cluttering your single screen with dozens of overlapping windows turns simple writing tasks into chaos. When your workspace is disorganized, you spend valuable mental energy alt-tabbing instead of making actual progress. Press Windows Key plus Arrow to snap active programs into clean two-window or four-window quadrants. You will keep your workspace neat and productive.",
